ogles2 (ports/gl4es): a program's built-in matrix uniforms are not sent
again while the matrices are unchanged; no uniform calls for absent units.

realize_glenv sent every built-in matrix uniform at every draw: the MVP
product, a hash lookup and a 64-byte compare per matrix, and the loop over
all texture units' matrices, about 5 us a draw on a 68k under Emu68
(Quake III: 0.7 ms a frame). matrix.c now bumps a generation whenever a
matrix's value changes (not for a glLoadIdentity of an identity matrix or a
glLoadMatrixf of the same values: Quake III resets its texture matrices
around every stage), and a program skips the block while the generation,
the glstate and the normal rescaling are those it last sent them with
(cleared at link). The texture-environment and sampler loops call
GoUniform* only for uniforms the program has (16 units, three calls each).

